## Cold start

Before acting in a new session, read:

```text
AGENTS.md
→ project_context.md
→ current_work.md
→ decision_log.md
→ artifact_index.md
```

Read `changelog.md` only when history matters. Use `artifact_index.md` to find detailed sources, and read them only when the current task touches their scope.

## Source roles

```text
Collaboration and safety rules       → AGENTS.md
Stable confirmed project truth       → project_context.md
Project-level progress and blockers  → current_work.md
Durable confirmed project decisions  → decision_log.md
Artifact and source navigation       → artifact_index.md
Effective substantive history        → changelog.md
Detailed domain facts                → sources registered in artifact_index.md
Task, checklist, issue, and QA status → corresponding execution source
Non-authoritative reference/history  → archive/
```

## Read and change safely

- Read the source that owns a fact before editing it.
- Preserve existing work and unrelated changes.
- Separate user-confirmed facts, source evidence, recommendations, and unknowns.
- Do not infer confirmed requirements, decisions, ownership, approvals, or project scope.
- Do not read or expose secrets. Do not recursively inspect large or generated assets.
- If sources conflict, stop the conflicting change, identify both sources, and request resolution.
- If required context cannot be read, do not modify affected critical material.

## Route updates by meaning

```text
Stable project state or constraint    → project_context.md or its domain source
Current project objective or blocker  → current_work.md
Durable confirmed project choice      → decision_log.md, pointing to detail
Detailed requirement or design        → its registered domain source
Task, checklist, issue, or test status → its registered execution source
Effective substantive change          → changelog.md
Artifact lifecycle or navigation      → artifact_index.md
Reusable collaboration safeguard      → AGENTS.md
Background or superseded material     → archive/
```

Update only files whose owned facts changed. Pure discussion, rejected drafts, and formatting-only edits normally do not enter governance history.

## Project-level and work-item boundary

- A Checklist, Task, Todo, Issue, plan, launch guide, migration note, or other work-item document owns only its declared scope.
- A work-item stage is not the whole-project stage. A work-item choice is not a project decision.
- Promote a work-item fact only when the user or an explicitly canonical project-level source confirms its broader scope.
- Do not place business workflow details, task stages, checklist IDs, feature rules, or domain plans in this file.

## Asset placement

- Reserve the project root for governance entry points, confirmed project-level anchors, and tool-required files.
- Follow the detailed directory map in `artifact_index.md`.
- Place new assets automatically when their role and destination are unambiguous.
- Do not create empty directories for hypothetical future needs.
- Do not copy external canonical sources locally merely to fit the directory structure.
- Ask before moving, renaming, deleting, or archiving existing assets unless the user already approved the exact placement preview.

